  • Script complexity (Devanagari with complex sandhi rules)
  • Multi-task requirement (translation, QA, explanation, grammar)
  • Compute constraints (T4/L4 GPU, ≤16GB VRAM)

Core difficulty: Sanskrit is not a typical low-resource language —
it has extensive written resources, but most are NOT in modern NLP
training datasets. The challenge is not data scarcity but data FORMAT:
most Sanskrit data exists as raw text, not instruction-response pairs.

