5. HARDWARE CONSTRAINTS & OPTIMIZATIONS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Target Hardware: T4 GPU (16GB VRAM)

Memory budget:
  ┌─────────────────────────────┬──────────┐
  │ Component                   │ VRAM     │
  ├─────────────────────────────┼──────────┤
  │ Model weights (4-bit)       │ ~1.5 GB  │
  │ LoRA adapters (fp16)        │ ~0.2 GB  │
  │ Activations (batch=4,seq=512│ ~3.5 GB  │
  │ Gradient checkpointing saves│ -1.5 GB  │
  │ Optimizer (paged to CPU)    │ ~1.0 GB  │
  │ Framework overhead          │ ~1.0 GB  │
  ├─────────────────────────────┼──────────┤
  │ Total estimated             │ ~5.7 GB  │
  │ T4 available                │ 16.0 GB  │
  │ Headroom                    │ ~10 GB ✓ │
  └─────────────────────────────┴──────────┘

Optimizations applied:
  1. 4-bit NF4 quantization: 4× memory reduction vs fp32
  2. Double quantization: saves additional ~0.4 GB
  3. Gradient checkpointing: recomputes activations, saves ~40% memory
  4. paged_adamw: offloads optimizer states to CPU RAM
  5. group_by_length: reduces padding waste by batching similar lengths
  6. fp16 training: halves activation memory vs fp32

Training time estimate on T4:
  ~350 examples × 5 epochs / (4 batch × 8 grad_accum)
  = ~55 gradient steps total
  ≈ 30-45 minutes on T4

For L4 (24GB VRAM):
  - Could use bf16 instead of fp16 (more stable)
  - Could increase batch size to 8
  - Could use r=32 or r=64 for better quality
  - Flash Attention 2 available (2× speed improvement)

